            "success": "1765433524551"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5266,
            "y": 5945
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770753930605",
          "id": "1770739456446",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770739456449_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a high-precision Intent Classifier for a Payment Financing Assistant.\n\n### INPUTS\nInput Message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \nChat History: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} \n\n### OBJECTIVE\nAnalyze the Input Message to determine user intent. Use the Chat History ONLY for context (e.g., resolving pronouns like \"show me *those* programs\" to a previously mentioned category).\n\nYou must extract five key parameters based on the following rules:\n\n### 1. showTable (Boolean)\nSet to `true` ONLY when the user explicitly asks to view, show, list, display, or see a directory/table of the actual available financing program records.\n- Includes broad listing requests (\"show all programs\", \"what programs do I have?\").\n- Includes filtered listing requests (\"show virtual card programs\").\n- Set to `false` if the user is asking for descriptive details, specific attributes, terms, general knowledge, or conceptual questions about a financing option (e.g., \"I need the rebate details for...\", \"what is...\", \"explain...\", \"how does this work?\"). \n- IMPORTANT: Asking to generate a list of programs = `true`. Asking for explanatory text or specific descriptive details about a program type = `false`.\n\nAvailable program listing rule:\nIf the user asks to list, review, show, view, or see available financing programs, payment programs, financing options, payment options, or financing program types, set showTable = true.\n\nTreat these as available-program directory requests, not conceptual explanation requests.\n\nThis includes provider/company wording such as:\n- programs offered by Oracle\n- programs provided by Oracle\n- programs Oracle offers\n- available financing programs\n- review my available financing programs\n\nFor these requests:\n- showTable = true\n- financingProgramCategories = [\"all\"]\n- financingProgramTypes = [\"all\"]\n- financingProgramNames = []\n\nIf the user asks for a brief, overview, explanation, summary, or description of programs, set showTable = false even if the request contains words like available, offered, or Oracle offers.\n\nSet showTable = true only when the user is asking to list, show, view, display, see, or enumerate the actual financing program records.\n\nProgram type availability rule:\nIf the user asks which financing program types, payment program types, financing options, or payment options Oracle offers, provides, supports, or has available, set showTable = true.\n\nTreat these as available-program listing requests, not conceptual explanation requests.\n\nExamples:\n- \"Which financing program types does Oracle offer?\" -> showTable=true, financingProgramCategories=[\"all\"], financingProgramTypes=[\"all\"]\n- \"What payment program types are available?\" -> showTable=true, financingProgramCategories=[\"all\"], financingProgramTypes=[\"all\"]\n- \"Which financing options do I have?\" -> showTable=true, financingProgramCategories=[\"all\"], financingProgramTypes=[\"all\"]\n\nBenefit comparison rule:\nIf the user asks to compare benefits, explain differences, compare suitability, compare working capital impact, or compare how financing option types work, set `showTable` to `false`.\n\nProgram category comparison rule:\nIf the user compares program categories using \"vs\", \"versus\", \"difference between\", or \"compare\", such as offered vs signed programs, signed vs external programs, or offered vs external programs, set showTable = false.\n\nThis applies even if the message starts with \"list\" or \"show\", because the user is asking for a comparison/explanation between categories, not a directory table.\n\nStill extract the mentioned categories and program type.\n\nProgram category comparison rule:\nIf the user compares program categories using \"vs\", \"versus\", \"difference between\", or \"compare\", such as offered vs signed programs, signed vs external programs, or offered vs external programs, set showTable = false.\n\nThis applies even if the message starts with \"list\" or \"show\", because the user is asking for a comparison/explanation between categories, not a directory table.\n\nStill extract the mentioned categories and program type.\n\nExamples of descriptive comparison intent that MUST set `showTable` to `false`:\n- \"Compare the benefits of Dynamic Discounting and Virtual Card programs\"\n- \"What is the difference between Virtual Cards and Dynamic Discounting?\"\n- \"Which is better for cash flow, Virtual Cards or Dynamic Discounting?\"\n\nOnly set `showTable` to `true` for comparison requests when the user explicitly asks to compare actual available program records, such as:\n- \"Compare my available Virtual Card programs\"\n- \"Show a comparison of signed and external Dynamic Discounting programs\"\n- \"List the available programs and compare them\"\n\n### 2. isSCFQuery (Boolean)\nSet to `true` ONLY when the user explicitly mentions \"Supply Chain Financing\" or \"SCF\" (case-insensitive). Otherwise, `false`.\n\n### 3. financingProgramNames (Array of Strings)\nExtract specific, proper financing program name(s) explicitly mentioned in the Input Message (e.g., \"Global Bank Early Pay\").\n- Do NOT extract general categories or types (e.g., \"external\", \"vcc\", \"virtual card\", \"dd\", \"offered\", \"scf\") as names.\n- Return the raw user-facing labels, normalized ONLY for lowercase. Do not force these into the enum categories.\n- If more than one proper name is mentioned, return all of them.\n- FALLBACK: If no specific proper financing program name can be explicitly identified from the input message, return `[]`. Do not return \"all\" for names.\n\n### 4. financingProgramCategories (Array of Strings)\nMap the identified financing programs to their corresponding system categories.\n- FIXED ENUM LIST: `all`, `external`, `signed`, `offered`\n- If more than one category is mentioned, return all matching values.\n- FALLBACK: If `showTable` is `true` but no specific category can be identified from the input, return `[\"all\"]`.\n\nProvider wording availability rule:\nIf the user says programs \"offered by Oracle\", \"provided by Oracle\", \"available from Oracle\", \"supported by Oracle\", \"Oracle offers\", \"Oracle provides\", or similar provider/company wording, treat this as a request for all available financing programs.\n\nFor these requests:\n- financingProgramCategories = [\"all\"]\n- financingProgramTypes = [\"all\"]\n- showTable = true\n\nDo not interpret the word \"offered\" in \"offered by Oracle\" as the program category \"offered\".\nOnly use financingProgramCategories = [\"offered\"] when the user clearly asks for offered financing programs as a category, such as \"offered programs\", \"offered financing programs\", or \"program type offered\".\n\n### 5. financingProgramTypes (Array of Strings)\nMap the identified financing programs to their corresponding instrument types.\n- FIXED ENUM LIST: `all`, `vcc`, `dynamic_discounting`\n- NORMALIZATION MAPPING:\n  - \"virtual card\" OR \"vcc\" -> `vcc`\n  - \"dynamic discounting\" OR \"dd\" -> `dynamic_discounting`\n- If more than one type is mentioned, return all matching values.\n- FALLBACK: If `showTable` is `true` but no specific type can be identified from the input, return `[\"all\"]`.\n\n### EXAMPLES\n\nInput: \"show all available financingPrograms\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"all\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"all\"]}\n\nInput: \"I need the rebate details for the virtual card financing option.\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": false, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"vcc\"]}\n\nInput: \"What are my available external VCC programs?\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"external\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"vcc\"]}\n\nInput: \"show virtual card and dd programs\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"all\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"vcc\", \"dynamic_discounting\"]}\n\nInput: \"show external and signed dd programs\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"external\", \"signed\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"dynamic_discounting\"]}\n\nInput: \"show me details for the Global Bank Virtual Card program\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [\"global bank virtual card\"], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"all\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"all\"]}\n\nInput: \"hello there\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": false, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [], \"financingProgramTypes\": []}\n\nInput: \"List offered versus signed Dynamic Discounting programs.\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": false, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"offered\", \"signed\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"dynamic_discounting\"]}\n\nInput: \"Compare signed and offered DD programs.\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": false, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"signed\", \"offered\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"dynamic_discounting\"]}\n\nInput: \"List the different financing programs offered by Oracle.\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"all\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"all\"]}\n\nInput: \"show all available financingPrograms\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"all\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"all\"]}\n\nInput: \"Review my available financing programs.\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"all\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"all\"]}\n\nInput: \"Which financing program types are available from Oracle?\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": true, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"all\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"all\"]}\n\nInput: \"Compare signed and offered DD programs.\"\nOutput: {\"showTable\": false, \"isSCFQuery\": false, \"financingProgramNames\": [], \"financingProgramCategories\": [\"signed\", \"offered\"], \"financingProgramTypes\": [\"dynamic_discounting\"]}\n\n\n### OUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn EXACTLY ONE valid JSON object. Do not repeat the output, do not include markdown formatting (no ```json wrapper), and do not include any conversational text. Use exactly these keys:\n{\n  \"showTable\": boolean,\n  \"isSCFQuery\": boolean,\n  \"financingProgramNames\": string[],\n  \"financingProgramCategories\": string[],\n  \"financingProgramTypes\": string[]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"description\": \"Determines if the Financing Programs Table should be shown, whether the query specifically relates to Supply Chain Financing (SCF), and extracts specific program names, categories, and types.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"showTable\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Indicates whether the user query requests financing program information. True if the query asks for available programs, specific program types, program details, comparisons, or tables; false otherwise.\"\n    },\n    \"isSCFQuery\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Indicates whether the user query specifically mentions Supply Chain Financing or its abbreviation SCF.\"\n    },\n    \"financingProgramNames\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"Specific, proper financing program name(s) explicitly mentioned by the user (e.g., 'Global Bank Early Pay'). Do NOT extract general categories or types here. Default to an empty array [] if no specific proper name is mentioned.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"financingProgramCategories\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"The system category(ies) explicitly mentioned by the user. If the query is about financing programs but no category can be identified, return [\\\"all\\\"].\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"all\",\n          \"external\",\n          \"signed\",\n          \"offered\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"financingProgramTypes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"The financing instrument type(s) explicitly mentioned by the user. If the query is about financing programs but no type can be identified, return [\\\"all\\\"].\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"all\",\n          \"vcc\",\n          \"dynamic_discounting\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"showTable\",\n    \"isSCFQuery\",\n    \"financingProgramNames\",\n    \"financingProgramCategories\",\n    \"financingProgramTypes\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Financing Programs Information Formatter",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "/*************************************************\n * INPUT DATA\n *************************************************/\nconst programs = ($context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BO_RETRIEVE_FINANCING_PROGRAM.$output.items || [])\n  .filter(p => p.financingOptionTypeCode !== \"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\");\n\nconst ragData = Array.isArray($context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_RAG_CONTENT_FORMATTER.$output)\n  ? $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_RAG_CONTENT_FORMATTER.$output\n  : [];\n\n/*************************************************\n * HELPER FUNCTIONS\n *************************************************/\n/**\n * Returns RAG entry matching exact program name AND financingProgramCode\n */\nconst getRagByProgramNameAndCode = (programName, programCode) => {\n  if (!programName) return null;\n  \n  const targetName = programName.toLowerCase().trim();\n  const targetCode = (programCode || \"\").toLowerCase().trim();\n\n  return ragData.find(r =>\n    (r.program_name || \"\").toLowerCase().trim() === targetName &&\n    (r.program_code || \"\").toLowerCase().trim() === targetCode\n  ) || null;\n};\n\n/*************************************************\n * SPLIT PROGRAMS FROM API\n *************************************************/\n// Programs that are offered but not necessarily signed\nconst offeredProgramsFromAPI = programs.filter(p => {\n  const programTypeId = p.programType?.$id || \"\";\n  return (\n    programTypeId.includes(\"OFFERED_PARTNER_PROGRAM\") ||\n    programTypeId.includes(\"ORA_CE_OFFERED_FIN_PROGRAM\")\n  );\n});\n\n// Programs that are already signed\nconst signedProgramsFromAPI = programs.filter(p => {\n  const programTypeId = p.programType?.$id || \"\";\n  return programTypeId.includes(\"SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAM\");\n});\n\nconst signedFinancingOptionTypes = new Set(\n  signedProgramsFromAPI.map(p => p.financingOptionTypeCode).filter(Boolean)\n);\n\n/*************************************************\n * BUILD OFFERED PROGRAMS LIST\n *************************************************/\nconst offeredPrograms = [\n  ...(!signedFinancingOptionTypes.has(\"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\")\n    ? [{\n        program_name: \"Virtual card\",\n        financing_option_type: \"Virtual credit card program\",\n        financing_option_type_code: \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\",\n        program_type: \"Offered financing program\",\n        additional_info: \"N/A\"\n      }]\n    : []),\n  ...offeredProgramsFromAPI\n    .filter(p => !signedFinancingOptionTypes.has(p.financingOptionTypeCode))\n    .map(p => ({\n      program_name: p.name || null,\n      financing_option_type: p.financingOptionType?.meaning || null,\n      financing_option_type_code: p.financingOptionTypeCode || null,\n      program_type: p.programType?.meaning || null,\n      program_id: p.financingProgramId,\n      additional_info: \"N/A\"\n    }))\n];\n\n/*************************************************\n * BUILD SIGNED PROGRAMS (WITH RAG ENRICHMENT)\n *************************************************/\nconst signedPrograms = signedProgramsFromAPI.map(p => {\n  const optionTypeText = (p.financingOptionType?.meaning || \"\").toLowerCase();\n\n  // -------- RAG MATCH --------\n  const ragMatch = getRagByProgramNameAndCode(p.name, p.financingProgramCode);\n\n  // -------- API NATIVE INFO --------\n  const apiInfo = {\n    maximum_discount_rate: p.maximumDiscountRate || null,\n    minimum_discount_rate: p.minimumDiscountRate || null,\n    default_discount_rate: p.defaultDiscountRate || null\n  };\n\n  // -------- RAG INFO --------\n  const ragInfo = ragMatch?.details || {};\n\n  // -------- MERGED ADDITIONAL INFO --------\n  const additionalInfo = { ...apiInfo, ...ragInfo };\n\n  return {\n    program_name: p.name || null,\n    financing_option_type: p.financingOptionType?.meaning || null,\n    financing_option_type_code: p.financingOptionTypeCode || null,\n    program_type: p.programType?.meaning || null,\n    program_id: p.financingProgramId,\n    additional_info: additionalInfo\n  };\n});\n\n/*************************************************\n * DETERMINE UNSIGNED OFFERED PROGRAMS\n *************************************************/\nconst signedParentProgramIds = signedProgramsFromAPI\n  .map(p => p.parentFinancingProgram?.financingProgramId)\n  .filter(Boolean);\n\nconst unsignedOfferedPrograms = offeredProgramsFromAPI\n  .filter(p => !signedParentProgramIds.includes(p.financingProgramId))\n  .map(p => ({\n    program_name: p.name,\n    financing_option_type: p.financingOptionType?.meaning || null,\n    financing_option_type_code: p.financingOptionTypeCode || null,\n    program_type: p.programType?.meaning || null\n  }));\n\n/*************************************************\n * EXTERNAL FINANCING PROGRAMS (from RAG only)\n *************************************************/\n\n// 1. Create the composite keys from the API programs (Name | Code)\nconst systemProgramKeys = new Set(programs.map(p => \n  `${(p.name || \"\").toLowerCase().trim()}|${(p.financingProgramCode || \"\").toLowerCase().trim()}`\n));\n\nconst externalPrograms = ragData\n  .filter(rag => {\n    // 2. Get the name and code from the RAG data\n    const ragName = (rag.program_name || \"\").toLowerCase().trim();\n    // (Assuming your RAG data uses financing_program_code to match the API. If it uses something else, update this line)\n    const ragCode = (rag.program_code || \"\").toLowerCase().trim(); \n    \n    // 3. Combine them into the same format\n    const compositeKey = `${ragName}|${ragCode}`;\n    \n    // 4. Check the composite key against our Set\n    return (\n      ragName && \n      !systemProgramKeys.has(compositeKey) && \n      rag.financing_option_type_code !== \"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\"\n    );\n  })\n  .map(rag => ({\n    program_name: rag.program_name || null,\n    financing_option_type: rag.financing_option_type || \"N/A\",\n    financing_option_type_code: rag.financing_option_type_code || null,\n    program_type: \"External financing program\",\n    program_id: null,\n    additional_info: rag.details || {}\n  }));\n/*************************************************\n * FORMAT OUTPUT\n *************************************************/\nconst input = {\n  offered_programs: offeredPrograms,\n  signed_programs: signedPrograms,\n  unsigned_offered_programs: unsignedOfferedPrograms\n};\n\nconst parseInput = typeof input === \"string\" ? JSON.parse(input) : input;\n\nconst allPrograms = [\n  ...(parseInput.offered_programs || []),\n  ...(parseInput.signed_programs || []),\n  ...externalPrograms\n];\n\n/*************************************************\n * FILTERING LOGIC (INTENT CLASSIFICATION)\n *************************************************/\nlet finalPrograms = [...allPrograms];\n\nconst intentOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_CLASSIFIER.$output || {};\nconst intentNames = Array.isArray(intentOutput.financingProgramNames) ? intentOutput.financingProgramNames : [];\nconst intentCats = Array.isArray(intentOutput.financingProgramCategories) ? intentOutput.financingProgramCategories : [];\nconst intentTypes = Array.isArray(intentOutput.financingProgramTypes) ? intentOutput.financingProgramTypes : [];\n\n// 1. Program Name Precedence\nlet nameMatched = false;\nif (intentNames.length > 0 && !intentNames.includes(\"all\")) {\n  const lowerNames = intentNames.map(n => n.toLowerCase().trim());\n  const nameFiltered = finalPrograms.filter(p =>\n    p.program_name && lowerNames.includes(p.program_name.toLowerCase().trim())\n  );\n  \n  if (nameFiltered.length > 0) {\n    finalPrograms = nameFiltered;\n    nameMatched = true;\n  }\n}\n\n// 2. Fallback to Categories & Types Filtering\nif (!nameMatched) {\n  const filterCats = intentCats.length > 0 && !intentCats.includes(\"all\");\n  const filterTypes = intentTypes.length > 0 && !intentTypes.includes(\"all\");\n\n  if (filterCats || filterTypes) {\n    finalPrograms = finalPrograms.filter(prog => {\n      let catMatch = true;\n      let typeMatch = true;\n\n      // Evaluate Categories (OR logic within categories)\n      if (filterCats) {\n        catMatch = false; // reset to false so it must match at least one\n        if (intentCats.includes(\"external\") && prog.program_type === \"External financing program\") catMatch = true;\n        if (intentCats.includes(\"signed\") && prog.program_type === \"Signed financing program\") catMatch = true;\n        if (intentCats.includes(\"offered\") && prog.program_type && prog.program_type.startsWith(\"Offered\")) catMatch = true;\n      }\n\n      // Evaluate Types (OR logic within types)\n      if (filterTypes) {\n        typeMatch = false; // reset to false so it must match at least one\n        if (intentTypes.includes(\"vcc\") && prog.financing_option_type_code === \"VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD\") typeMatch = true;\n        if (intentTypes.includes(\"dynamic_discounting\") && prog.financing_option_type_code === \"DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING\") typeMatch = true;\n        if (intentTypes.includes(\"scf\") && prog.financing_option_type_code === \"SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING\") typeMatch = true;\n      }\n\n      // Both conditions must pass to be included (AND logic between groups)\n      return catMatch && typeMatch;\n    });\n  }\n}\n\n/*************************************************\n * RENDER TABLE\n *************************************************/\nconst formatAdditionalInfo = (info) => {\n  if (!info || typeof info !== \"object\") return \"\";\n\n  const parts = [];\n\n  const toReadable = (key) =>\n    key.replace(/_/g, \" \").replace(/\\b\\w/g, c => c.toUpperCase());\n\n  const formatValue = (key, value) => {\n    if (value === null || value === \"\") return \"\";\n    if (key.toLowerCase().endsWith(\"rate\")) {\n      return `${value}%`;\n    }\n    return value;\n  };\n\n  if (\n    info.maximum_discount_rate ||\n    info.minimum_discount_rate ||\n    info.default_discount_rate\n  ) {\n\nconst fmt = v =>\n  Number.isInteger(Math.round(Number(v) * 100) / 100)\n    ? String(Math.round(Number(v) * 100) / 100)\n    : (Math.round(Number(v) * 100) / 100).toFixed(2).replace(/\\.?0+$/, '');\n    \nconst min = fmt(info.minimum_discount_rate);\nconst max = fmt(info.maximum_discount_rate);\nconst def = fmt(info.default_discount_rate);\n\nparts.push(`Discount range: min ${min}% — max ${max}% (default ${def}%)`);\n\n    delete info.maximum_discount_rate;\n    delete info.minimum_discount_rate;\n    delete info.default_discount_rate;\n  }\n\n  Object.entries(info).forEach(([key, value]) => {\n    if (\n      value === null ||\n      value === \"\" ||\n      (Array.isArray(value) && value.length === 0)\n    ) {\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const readableKey = toReadable(key);\n\n    if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n      const formattedArray = value\n        .map(obj =>\n          Object.entries(obj)\n            .filter(([_, v]) => v !== null && v !== \"\")\n            .map(([k, v]) => `${toReadable(k)}: ${formatValue(k, v)}`)\n            .join(\", \")\n        )\n        .join(\" | \");\n\n      parts.push(`${readableKey}: ${formattedArray}`);\n    } else if (typeof value === \"object\") {\n      const formattedObj = Object.entries(value)\n        .filter(([_, v]) => v !== null && v !== \"\")\n        .map(([k, v]) => `${toReadable(k)}: ${formatValue(k, v)}`)\n        .join(\", \");\n\n      parts.push(`${readableKey}: ${formattedObj}`);\n    } else {\n      parts.push(`${readableKey}: ${formatValue(key, value)}`);\n    }\n  });\n\n  return parts.join(\", \");\n};\n\nconst tableContent = finalPrograms.map(program => ({\n  \"Program Name\": program.program_name || \"\",\n  \"Financing Option Type\": program.financing_option_type || \"\",\n  \"Program Type\": program.program_type || \"\",\n  \"Additional info\": formatAdditionalInfo(program.additional_info)\n}));\n\nlet summary = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_USER_INTENT_CLASSIFIER.$output.isSCFQuery ? \"I do not currently support the evaluation or listing of SCF programs. However, I can show you the other financing programs currently available in the system.\" : \"Here are the payment programs currently available to you.\";\n\nconst hasExternalPrograms = finalPrograms.some(p => p.program_type === \"External financing program\");\n\nlet seq = 1;\n\nconst result = [\n  {\n    type: \"text\",\n    content: [summary],\n    sequence: seq++\n  },\n  {\n    type: \"table\",\n    heading: \"Financing Program Details\",\n    content: tableContent,\n    sequence: seq++,\n    columnOrder: [\n      \"Program Name\",\n      \"Financing Option Type\",\n      \"Program Type\",\n      \"Additional info\"\n    ]\n  },\n  ...(hasExternalPrograms\n    ? [\n        {\n          type: \"text\",\n          content: [\n            \"Note: External programs are for analysis only and cannot be used to create offers.\"\n          ],\n          sequence: seq++\n        }\n      ]\n    : []),\n  {\n    type: \"text\",\n    content: [\n      \"Next Step: Evaluate payment opportunities for a specific signed program with the upcoming payments.\"\n    ],\n    formatHint: \"Make string Next Step BOLD\",\n    sequence: seq++\n  }\n];\n\nreturn result;\n"
          },
