          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5038.3233467248065,
            "y": 5363.646956096973
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_RAG_CONTENT_FORMATTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769687861342",
          "id": "1765433257290",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765433257292_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You will be given a JSON produced from the Financing_Programs_RAG_Supplemental tool.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- This JSON may vary in structure because it is created by an LLM.\n- Your task is to normalize this JSON into a FIXED TEMPLATE OBJECT that always follows the structure defined below.\n- Output ONLY valid JSON. No explanations, no natural language.\n\nFIXED TEMPLATE YOU MUST RETURN -\nReturn a JSON array. Each element must be exactly:\n\n{\n  \"financing_option_type\": \"<Virtual credit card program | Supply chain financing program | Dynamic discounting program | Unknown>\",\n  \"financing_option_type_code\": \"<VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD | SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING | DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING | Unknown>\",\n  \"program_name\": \"<string or null>\",\n  \"program_code\": \"<string or null>\",\n  \"details\": {\n      \"market_borrowing_interest_rate\": \"<string or null>\",\n      \"market_short_term_investment_rate\": \"<string or null>\",\n      \"rebate_rates\": [\n         {\n           \"rcn\": \"<string>\",\n           \"rebate_rate\": \"<string or null>\"\n         }\n      ]\n  }\n}\n\nMAPPING RULES -\n1. Explicitly translate the incoming financing type to EXACTLY one of the following strings for the \"financing_option_type\" field:\n   - If input is \"Virtual Card\" or similar -> map to \"Virtual credit card program\"\n   - If input is \"Dynamic Discounting\" or similar -> map to \"Dynamic discounting program\"\n   - If input is \"Supply Chain Financing\" or similar -> map to \"Supply chain financing program\"\n   If the incoming value is unclear or does not match, map to \"Unknown\".\n\n2. Always map the \"financing_option_type_code\" to the corresponding uppercase enum: VIRTUAL_CREDIT_CARD, DYNAMIC_DISCOUNTING, SUPPLY_CHAIN_FINANCING, or Unknown.\n\n3. Always return:\n   - program_name (string or null)\n   - program_code (string or null)\n\n4. Always return a details object containing ALL THREE fields:\n   - market_borrowing_interest_rate\n   - market_short_term_investment_rate\n   - rebate_rates (array)\n   Even if the input LLM JSON is missing a section.\n\n5. Populate details using rules:\n   - For \"Virtual credit card program\":\n        * market_borrowing_interest_rate → from input if present else null\n        * rebate_rates → normalize input array; if missing, return empty array\n        * market_short_term_investment_rate → null\n   - For \"Dynamic discounting program\":\n        * market_short_term_investment_rate → value or null\n        * market_borrowing_interest_rate → null\n        * rebate_rates → []\n\n  5A. RCN extraction rule:\n  When extracting details.rebate_rates[].rcn, use the RCN identifier itself, not the alias name.\n  \n  If the source contains text like:\n  \"RCN-A Alias Name: Corporate Card Group\"\n  then set:\n  \"rcn\": \"RCN-A\"\n  \n  If the source contains text like:\n  \"VC-RCN-USD Alias Name: North America Card Alias\"\n  then set:\n  \"rcn\": \"VC-RCN-USD\"\n  \n  If the source contains text like:\n  \"Real Card Number RCN-200 Alias: EMEA Payment Alias\"\n  then set:\n  \"rcn\": \"RCN-200\"\n  \n  Do not set rcn to the alias name after \"Alias Name\" or \"Alias\".\n  Do not use alias labels such as \"Corporate Card Group\", \"North America Card Alias\", or \"EMEA Payment Alias\" as rcn values.\n  The alias name may be ignored unless the fixed template explicitly has a separate alias field.\n  \n6. If input contains extra fields, ignore them.\n7. If the input JSON contains multiple programs, normalize ALL of them.\n\nINPUT FORMAT -\nThe input value will be an object, an array, or LLM free-form JSON.\nYou must parse it safely and return the normalized fixed template.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT REQUIREMENTS -\n- Output MUST be valid JSON.\n- Output MUST be an array of fixed template objects.\n- No text, no comments, only JSON.\n\nNow normalize {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_RAG_FINANCING_PROGRAM_PROCESSOR.$output.value}} into the FIXED TEMPLATE JSON format."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
